mission "The Monk Who Burned His Maps"
    name "The Monk Who Burned His Maps"
    description "Find Brother Mateo, who has been hiding a forbidden chart from a royal collector."
    source "Gallows Key"
    destination "San Aurelio"
    reward 810
    speaker offer "Brother Mateo"
    speaker visit "Brother Mateo"
    speaker complete "Brother Mateo"
    to offer
        has "The Observatory's Blue Flame: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Brother Mateo keeps the door barred. A bundle of map fragments smoulders in the brazier, while one chart remains hidden beneath a stack of monastery papers.`
            `Brother Mateo glances toward the door. "A royal collector has been asking after this chart. I burned the copies, but I will not destroy the original until I know why the expedition needed it hidden."`
            choice
                `"You have my attention. What needs doing first?"`
                    accept
                `"Who stands to gain if the truth stays buried?"`
                    goto details
                `"I have no wish to become a pawn in someone else's quarrel."`
                    close
            label details
                `He places one finger on the western edge of the surviving map. "This passage does not appear in the Crown's atlases. If the collector takes the chart, it will disappear into a private archive—and so will the only lead we have."`
                choice
                    `"All right. I will follow the evidence."`
                        accept
                    `"My answer has not changed. I will not sail."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Monk Who Burned His Maps. Find Brother Mateo, who has been hiding a forbidden chart from a royal collector."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At San Aurelio, Mateo unrolls the chart beneath a candle. The old marks lead to a place deliberately removed from official maps. "The expedition did not sail west for treasure alone," he says. "It was sent to find somewhere the authorities wanted forgotten."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Mateo rolls the chart carefully. "I will keep it safe, but it should belong neither to a collector nor to a monastery. The people who live beside that water have the first claim to its story."`
        log "Completed The Monk Who Burned His Maps. Received 810 gold. Find Brother Mateo, who has been hiding a forbidden chart from a royal collector."
